      "writtenOn": "2023-05-10T13:41:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we need to take dt into account for this use case.\nI\u0027ve found experimentally that dt doesn\u0027t change a lot - it stays within 198-204ms.\n\nLet `Ki\u0027 \u003d Ki*dt`\n\n```\nintegral +\u003d error * dt;\nresult +\u003d Ki * integral`;\n```\n\nis equivalent to\n```\nintegral +\u003d error;\nresult +\u003d Ki\u0027 * integral;\n```\n\nThe same logic applies to derivative part.\nSince dt is doesn\u0027t have significant variation we can silently omit it.\n\nNow with that being said if we want to provide a \"generic\" PID util we should take dt into account.\nI\u0027ll update the code.",
      "parentUuid": "45fb76c8_25cd73db",
      "revId": "1fa3775d6701fd5f9d9a304241324fd4f4d9b828",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1766249_facda5f8",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1395927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-10T12:29:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Derivative part is wrongly calculated!!!\n\nPlease follow the example, it is much simpler in form and easier to read.\n\n```\nfloat pid_controller(float error, float dt) {\n\n    integral +\u003d error * dt;\n    derivative \u003d (error - last_error) / dt;\n    last_error \u003d error;\n\n    return Kp * error + Ki * integral + Kd * derivative;\n}\n```",
      "revId": "1fa3775d6701fd5f9d9a304241324fd4f4d9b828",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
